# BrickOfTicks System — Comprehensive Understanding

## What Is This System?

**BrickOfTicks** is an **XAUUSD Renko trading system** that predicts whether price will hit Take Profit (TP) before Stop Loss (SL) after each Renko brick close, using **tick-level microstructure physics** (Order Flow Imbalance) fed into a **CNN+LSTM hybrid model** with dual prediction heads.

The core thesis: unfiltered Renko trading at 1:1 TP/SL yields ~49.5% win rate (slightly negative after spread). By filtering trades through **fast-brick hard rules** (87–94% WR) and a **microstructure model** (target ≥60% WR), the system achieves positive expected value.

---

## The Three Exploitable Inefficiencies

| Inefficiency | Win Rate | Condition | Mechanism |
|---|---|---|---|
| Duration momentum | 64–79% | Bricks forming in <10 seconds | Aggressive order flow continues |
| Sequence context | 87–94% | Fast bricks + Agreement ≥4 or ≤1 | Directional context amplifies signal |
| OFI microstructure | Target ≥60% | Normal bricks filtered by model | OFI predicts price impact (R²=65%) |

---

## Data Available

### Tick Data (`Data/Raw/Ticks/`)
- **Format**: Daily `.parquet` files organized as `Ticks/{year}/{month}/{day}.parquet`
- **Schema**: `timestamp` (ns, UTC), `bid`, `bid_vol`, `ask`, `ask_vol`
- **Coverage**: 2020–2026 (7 years)
- **Nature**: L1 OTC quote stream — **no trade prices** (Lee-Ready is invalid)

### Renko CSVs (`Data/Raw/`)
| File | Rows | Coverage |
|---|---|---|
| `renko_with_tick_outcomes_no_be_XAUUSD20-24.csv` | 30,978 | 2020–2024 |
| `renko_with_tick_outcomes_no_be_24_local.csv` | 6,169 | 2024 only |

**Columns**: `date`, `open`, `high`, `low`, `close`, `volume` (always 1.0), `uptrend`, `brick_size` (ATR-based, mean ~2.11), `sequence` (binary direction string), `outcome` (WIN/LOSS)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The CSVs contain only binary WIN/LOSS outcomes. They do **NOT** contain `y_mag` (overshoot ratio). Computing `y_mag` requires scanning L1 tick data after each brick close — this is a **hard dependency** for training Head B.

---

## The Prediction Target: Predicted Overshoot (Pred_OS)

**Pred_OS** = total price travel from entry to peak, normalised by `brick_size`. Measured from **entry price**, not from TP.

- `Pred_OS < 1.0` → LOSS (SL hit first)
- `Pred_OS = 1.0` → TP exactly reached
- `Pred_OS > 1.1` → TP reached + spread covered (trade filter threshold)

**Label construction** (`y_mag`):
- **WIN**: `y_mag = (peak_price - entry_price) / brick_size` (from L1 tick scan)
- **LOSS**: `y_mag = 0.0` (not masked — the model must learn to output zero for losing setups)

---

## System Architecture (5 Phases)

### Phase 1: Feature Engineering — The 9D Tick Vector + 3D Macro Vector

**Per-tick** (9 features, all z-scored over rolling 1000-tick window):

| # | Feature | Formula | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `z_OFI` | Weak-inequality OFI → z-score | Core pressure signal (Cont et al.) |
| 2 | `z_Depth` | bid_vol + ask_vol → z-score | Total liquidity at the touch |
| 3 | `z_Susc` | OFI_raw / (Depth_raw + 1e-8) → z-score | Pressure per unit resistance (divide RAW first, THEN z-score) |
| 4 | `z_Vel` | 1/(tick_gap_ms + 1e-3) → z-score | Tick arrival velocity |
| 5 | `z_Spread` | ask - bid → z-score | Dealer risk aversion indicator |
| 6 | `Progress` | (mid - brick_open) / brick_size | Price location within current brick (sawtooth) |
| 7 | `Flag_Curr` | 1 if tick ∈ current brick | Leakage guard (structural) |
| 8 | `Flag_Zone` | 1 if price is beyond prev brick's TP/SL | Leakage guard (surgical) |
| 9 | `Decay` | (CurrentBrickID - TickBrickID) / MaxDepth | Recency gradient (0=current, 1=oldest) |

**Per-brick** (3D macro-vector at brick close):

| # | Feature | Formula |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `Log_Dur` | log(duration_seconds + 1) |
| 2 | `Direction` | +1 (green) / -1 (red) |
| 3 | `z_Size` | (brick_size - μ_50) / σ_50 |

### Phase 2: Buffer Management & State Persistence

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Every Tick"] --> B["Micro-Buffer<br/>deque(maxlen=100)<br/>Stores 9D vectors"]
    A --> C["Z-Score Deques<br/>5× deque(maxlen=1000)<br/>Raw feature values"]
    D["Every Brick Close"] --> E["Macro-History<br/>Last 10 bricks<br/>RAW (100,9) snapshot + M_t"]
    D --> F["BrickID++"]
    G["Session Shutdown"] --> H["state.json<br/>Serialize all deques<br/>+ Macro-History"]
    H --> I["Session Startup<br/>Restore & recompute μ/σ"]
```

> [!NOTE]
> **Micro-Buffer is NEVER reset at brick boundaries**. It's a continuous rolling window. Fast bricks (~10 ticks) will have 90% spillover from prior bricks. The leakage flags (`Flag_Curr`, `Flag_Zone`, `Decay`) let the CNN distinguish current vs spillover ticks.

### Phase 3: Model Architecture — CNN + LSTM Hybrid

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Input"
        MT["Micro Tensor<br/>(B, 10, 100, 9)"]
        MV["Macro Tensor<br/>(B, 10, 3)"]
    end
    subgraph "Layer 1: TimeDistributed CNN (Microscope)"
        C1["Conv1D k=1, 16 filters (causal)"]
        C3["Conv1D k=3, 16 filters (causal)"]
        C5["Conv1D k=5, 16 filters (causal)"]
        CAT["Concat → (100, 48)"]
        MP["MaxPool1D(4) → (25, 48)"]
        FL["Flatten → Dense(32) → Dropout(0.3)"]
    end
    subgraph "Layer 2: Fusion"
        FUS["Concat CNN(32) + Macro(3) → (35) per brick"]
    end
    subgraph "Layer 3: LSTM (Telescope)"
        LSTM["LSTM(32, return_seq=False)<br/>→ Dropout(0.3)"]
    end
    subgraph "Layer 4: Dual Heads"
        HA["Head A: Dense(1, sigmoid)<br/>→ Prob_Win ∈ [0,1]"]
        HB["Head B: Dense(1, relu)<br/>→ Pred_OS ≥ 0"]
    end
    MT --> C1 & C3 & C5
    C1 & C3 & C5 --> CAT --> MP --> FL
    FL --> FUS
    MV --> FUS
    FUS --> LSTM
    LSTM --> HA & HB
```

**Key design decisions**:
- **MaxPool1D** (not GlobalAvgPool) — preserves temporal position within the 100-tick window
- **Causal padding** — no look-ahead within the buffer
- **Raw snapshots stored** (not pre-computed embeddings) — prevents train/inference batch norm mismatch
- **~48K total parameters** with ~24.5K training samples → 0.5:1 ratio → heavy regularization required

**Dual Prediction Heads** (both share the LSTM(32) output as input — no independent trunks):

| Head | Role | Activation | Output | What It Answers |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Head A** — Existence Classifier | Predicts probability of hitting TP before SL | `Dense(1, sigmoid)` | `Prob_Win ∈ [0.0, 1.0]` | *"Will this trade win?"* |
| **Head B** — Magnitude Regressor | Predicts total price travel from entry, normalised by brick_size | `Dense(1, relu)` | `Pred_OS ≥ 0` | *"How far will price go?"* |

Both heads must agree for a trade: `Prob_Win > 0.60` **AND** `Pred_OS > 1.1`. Head A filters low-confidence setups; Head B ensures the predicted move covers TP + spread cost. Training Head B on LOSS samples with `y_mag = 0.0` (rather than masking) teaches it to output near-zero for losing patterns — making Pred_OS a true expected-value predictor.

### Phase 4: Training Strategy

| Split | Date Range | Purpose | Size |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Train** | Jan 2020 – Dec 2022 | Weight learning | ~24,578 bricks |
| **Validation** | Jan 2023 – Mar 2023 | Threshold calibration | ~1,200 bricks |
| **Test** | Apr 2023 – Dec 2023 | Final eval (never opened) | ~3,600 bricks |

**Loss function**: `L = 1.0 × BCE(Prob_Win, y_class) + 0.3 × Huber(Pred_OS, y_mag, δ=1.0)`

**Exclusions**:
- Duration < 2s bricks excluded from training (handled by hard rule; buffers are ~95% spillover)
- Fast-brick chains > depth 5: `sample_weight = 0.5`

**Regularization**: Dropout(0.3), L2(1e-4), early stopping (patience=15), ReduceLROnPlateau

### Phase 5: Execution Logic

```
ON EVERY BRICK CLOSE:
  1. Update BrickID, store (100,9) snapshot + M_t in Macro-History
  2. IF system < Level 1 warmup  →  SKIP
  3. IF Duration < 10s:
       Agreement = count(last 5 bricks same direction as current)
       IF Agreement ≥ 4  →  ENTER in brick direction (trend)
       IF Agreement ≤ 1  →  ENTER in brick direction (reversal)
       IF Agreement = 2-3  →  SKIP
  4. IF Duration ≥ 10s AND system at Level 2:
       Build tensor (1,10,100,9) + macro (1,10,3)
       Model inference  →  Prob_Win, Pred_OS
       IF Prob_Win > 0.60 AND Pred_OS > 1.1  →  ENTER
       ELSE  →  SKIP
  5. IF entered: TP = entry ± 1×brick_size, SL = entry ∓ 1×brick_size
```

**Warmup levels**:
- **Level 1**: ≥5 bricks closed + ≥30 ticks → Hard Rule available
- **Level 2**: ≥10 bricks closed + 100 ticks in Micro-Buffer → Model inference available

**Order parameters**: Market entry at brick close, 1:1 TP/SL, **no early exit** (first-passage-time probability is the statistical basis of the edge).

---

## Acceptance Criteria (Key Items)

| AC | Criterion | Pass Condition |
|---|---|---|
| AC-01 | No look-ahead bias | Feature vector at tick k has zero info from k+1 onwards |
| AC-02 | OFI weak inequality | e_k non-zero when bid price static but volume changes |
| AC-05 | Walk-forward split integrity | Zero date overlap between splits |
| AC-09 | Head B correlation | Pearson r ≥ 0.30 on validation WIN samples |
| AC-11 | Hard rule win rate | ≥80% WR for Agreement ≥4 or ≤1 on test set |
| AC-12 | Model win rate | ≥60% WR on model-filtered bricks on test set |
| AC-13 | Inference latency | p99 < 100ms |

---

## Key Risks

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Model overfits 2020–2022 regime | Quarterly walk-forward retraining; retrain if 4-week WR < 52% |
| OTC volume always 1.0 | z_Depth/z_OFI become price-direction-only; Susceptibility still valid |
| Head B near-zero variance | Auto-fallback to binary classifier (y_mag > 1.2) |
| Pred_OS threshold insufficient if spread spikes | Live spread guard pauses trading when spread > 2× rolling mean |
| Fast brick chains saturate buffer | Chain downweighting (sample_weight = 0.5) |

---

## What Needs To Be Built

The project is at the **pre-implementation stage**. The PRD and Implementation Plan are fully specified. The data pipeline (Renko CSVs from tick data) already exists from prior work. What remains:

1. **Label Generation Pipeline** — Scan L1 ticks to compute `y_mag` for each brick
2. **Feature Engineering Module** — 9D tick vector computation with OFI weak inequalities
3. **Buffer Management** — Micro-Buffer, Macro-History, z-score persistence
4. **Model Architecture** — TimeDistributed CNN + LSTM with dual heads
5. **Training Pipeline** — Walk-forward split, hybrid loss, exclusions
6. **Execution Engine** — Warmup protocol, hard rule, model inference, order placement
7. **State Persistence** — `state.json` serialization/restoration
